From 89d5a120c087599344aed0e46fa9fe268b57d5a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:01:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] badgeui: fixes from a review of the day's changes

- A dump never replaces another. A new dump went on the newest saved
  card with its UID, often a duplicate: the copy then pointed at the
  original's file again, so editing the copy changed the original, and
  the copy's own file dropped out of Cards. A new dump now goes on a card
  with that UID that has no dump yet (saved from a search), else a new
  card; the app's own MIFARE Classic dump takes a free file name (-001,
  -002, as the client's newfilenamemcopy) instead of overwriting.
- An LF dump with a UID of its own (EM4x05, HITAG) went on the LF card
  searched last, whatever its ID: a saved EM410x became an EM4x05. Only a
  T55xx dump (no UID of its own) still goes on the searched card.
- HITAG's load ran lf hitag eload -2 at once; the client wants the Hitag
  type (-1, -2, -s, -m), so it is typed in the Console now.
- A type screen's %F (Load the dump, Restore) took the oldest saved card
  with the UID, of any type; now the newest of the type (a copy being
  edited, not its original).
- Duplicate from the card view left the list's focus on another card.
- Duplicate copies the whole file (it read at most 4 KB) and fails
  rather than overwrite when no "-copyN" name is free.
- An action's dump (hf mfu dump, ...) asked for the name before the
  result screen, which cleared "Saved to Cards".
- The host sim names its dumps as the client does (-001 when the file
  exists); two dead lines in the tests removed.

Tested: test_pm3ui.py 32/32 on the host (new: a dump never replaces
another, a card saved from a search gets the dump, an LF dump of another
chip, HITAG's load typed, the type screen loads the newest dump,
Duplicate from the card view); the review's three reproductions behave.
Not on the badge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
